From ced6df776e6f3af005b863ff4e2f6b11c70051d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladan Kovacevic <vkovacevic@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:44:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [feat] Opt-in unset top-k on device and async grammar
 reconciliation for host-sampled steps

agentic-models patch nanbeige_4_3_33b-plugin-sampling-routing.patch (Nanbeige4.3-33B bring-up,
vllm-tt-plugin nanbeige43-bringup 358ee85 and 7d2daa0, gated).

- supports_device_top_k_unset (default False): with a bounded max_device_top_k, an unset top-k
  (normalized to vocab_size) samples on device; explicit values above the bound keep the host route.
- reconcile_async_grammar_rows (default False): under async scheduling, a host-sampled submission
  uses the sample-time structured request set (as deferred device steps already do), so a request
  that retired while the step was in flight does not fail the strict mask remap.

Undeclared models keep the f6fe76b routing and grammar attach unchanged. The bring-up's duplicates of
the shared prefill-sampling-mask / original-prompt-lens patches are not carried, nor 6a7cc1d (numpy
views and one less block-table clone; its own measurement showed no throughput change).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
